cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use attenuo in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "attenuo: delegation-aware authorization and enforcement for tool-using AI agents"
abstract: >-
  A self-hosted reference monitor between AI agent clients and Model Context
  Protocol (MCP) tool servers. A user's login is exchanged (RFC 8693) for a
  delegation token that can only narrow at each hop; every proxied tool call is
  checked against every hop's lease, the chain's capabilities and run limits,
  and a Cedar policy that sees the call's arguments, and every decision is
  appended to a hash-chained audit log. Pre-alpha.
authors:
  - family-names: Kapoor
    given-names: Mudit
repository-code: "https://github.com/attenuo-dev/attenuo"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
keywords:
  - authorization
  - AI agents
  - Model Context Protocol
  - delegation
  - capabilities
  - Cedar
  - audit log
